the whole tech side of the internet is  going crazy over the leaks and rumors  for next year's macbook lineup since the  current lineup makes absolutely zero  sense with a killer value macbook air  for a thousand dollars than a terrible  value 1300 macbook pro which many people  agree shouldn't even exist and then a  massive 700 price gap going up to the  new 14 inch macbook pro for 2 000  but to make things even worse mark  german just came out with an extremely  controversial report claiming that apple  is not only adding another new m2  macbook air to the lineup but they're  upgrading the entry-level macbook pro  again with the same exact m2 chip  basically making it seem like the most  confusing report ever with many people  flat out saying that mark is wrong but  don't worry i've been giving this a lot  of thought and i think that i've finally  figured it all out so let's get right  into it first off mark german's report  says that five brand new macs are coming  in 2022 including a high-end imac an  updated mac mini and a new mac pro with  apple silicon all of which we've already  made full deep dive videos on so  definitely check them out if you haven't  already but in this video we've got to  discuss the 2022 macbook lineup because  everything else seems to make sense  compared to the macbook side which seems  like it's about to get more extensive  and confusing than ever before mark  german says that there's going to be a  new version of the entry-level macbook  pro which is something that many people  weren't expecting because the current  entry-level m1 model doesn't really have  a place in the lineup and i agree it  doesn't it's 300 more expensive than the  macbook air and it's not really much  faster at all in fact there are only a  few benefits like a touch bar which  nobody likes anyway a slightly brighter  500 nit display slightly better  microphones a faster 61 watt power  adapter and cooling fans which don't  really improve performance that much so  for the past few months especially after  the new m1 macbook pros were released  we've been literally telling people to  just buy the m1 macbook air instead of  the m1 macbook pro since you can get it  on sale right now on amazon for 900 and  get it shipped before christmas using  the link below and then if you really  want a macbook pro we've been telling  you guys just to go straight for the 14  inch for 2 000  completely skipping out on the m1  macbook pro altogether so the big  question is this why is mark german  saying that there's going to be a  refreshed macbook pro and how is it  going to fit into the 2022 macbook  lineup especially alongside the brand  new redesigned m2 macbook air which  everyone is so excited about so let's go  ahead and try to break it all down and  thankfully mark german has some older  reports that help piece this puzzle  together a few months back mark told us  that the entry-level macbook pro is  actually going to be getting the same  new m2 chip that's going to be going  into the macbook air which makes total  sense and then on top of that mark  german said that the new air will be  sold alongside the current m1 macbook  air so that means that it will not be  replacing it so it's simply going to be  a new more expensive m2 macbook air  model while the m1 model will likely  stick around at the same 999 price point  for another year and this actually makes  a whole lot of sense for apple to do  because it's exactly what they did in  2018 when they revealed the new  redesigned macbook air for  11.99 and still kept the old thick  silver bezel model around for a full  year at a 999 dollar price point and  then in 2019 apple dropped the base  price of the newly designed 2019 macbook  air by a hundred dollars so it started  at 10.99 while fully discontinuing the  old 999 dollar model and then finally in  early 2020 they released a new intel  based macbook air at that same  999 price point from before so over the  course of a couple of years apple  essentially phased out the old thousand  dollar macbook air and brought the newly  designed model down to that same  thousand dollar price point and i think  that's exactly what apple is gonna be  doing with the new m2 macbook air  releasing it at a higher price at first  while keeping the same old m1 macbook  air at 999  so the big question is this how is apple  gonna price both the new m2 macbook air  and the pro to make them make sense in  terms of a decent macbook lineup because  it's currently a bit confusing with the  m1 pro not really being worth it so what  is apple gonna change this time around  to actually make the m2 macbook pro  worth the extra cash over the m2 air  because in my opinion the pro absolutely  has to cost more than the air contrary  to the belief of some people who think  apple will be releasing a more expensive  15-inch macbook air which is based on  some old rumors and mark german has  already said that apple was thinking of  creating a 15-inch air but they  completely scrapped that idea and  they're not gonna do it anymore and if  you think about it a new macbook pro has  always been more expensive than a  macbook air it just makes sense from a  naming point of view so the main thing  we've gotta answer is how much the new  m2 macbook pro is gonna cost and why  would somebody pay the extra cash for it  over the air because recent reports are  already showing the new air to be a  killer upgrade with a full redesign that  looks absolutely beautiful and ming  choco fully believes that it's getting a  new mini led display which is actually  pretty surprising putting even more  pressure on the m2 macbook pro well for  starters apple could add in the same  benefits that the current m1 macbook pro  has over the m1 air like battery life  cooling fans to stop thermal throttling  a slightly brighter display slightly  better speakers and microphones and a  faster charging adapter but in reality  those differences alone aren't enough  because the current m1 pro is not worth  it compared to the air so the new lineup  obviously needs more differences for it  to make sense so let's get into the  changes that i personally think are  enough to make the future m2 macbook pro  worth it over the air first off i fully  believe that the new model is going to  be getting a full redesign just like the  m2 macbook air because if it sticks to  the current design absolutely nobody  would buy it over the new air it simply  makes no sense so with that said i think  it totally makes sense for the new m2  macbook pro to get the exact same  display and design as the 14 inch m1 pro  macbook pro the only difference would be  the lack of maybe some of the ports like  for example maybe one less thunderbolt  port or maybe the removal of the hdmi  port or something like that yes that  would obviously suck but it would push  people to spend more cash on the 2 000  m1 pro macbook pro which apple loves to  do on top of that i think this new entry  level m2 macbook pro would stick with  that beautiful 14 inch display with  120hz pro motion technology while the  new m2 air would likely only have a 13  inch display without the super thin  bezels and without 120hz promotion so  that display difference alone might be  enough to make people spend the extra  cash on the m2 macbook pro and then  finally we've got to talk about that new  m2 chip and the differences we'll see  between the air and the pro macbooks  mark german has already said that the m2  chip will essentially be the replacement  to the m1 with the same eight core cpu  with four high performance cores and  four efficiency cores but it's gonna  have a faster gpu with either nine or  ten gpu cores instead of the m1 that  goes up to eight with only seven on the  base model and one macbook air so i  think apple is gonna do exactly that  they're gonna give the m2 macbook air a  9 core gpu at the base model while  giving the mt macbook pro the full 10  gpu course and if you didn't already  know the current fanless macbook air  actually does throttle the performance  of the m1 chip a little bit so with the  m2 chip having more gpu cores the  macbook pro might actually have a  noticeable jump in performance next year  and then on top of that if the m2  macbook air gets off-white bezels like  all of the rumors are pointing to then  some people would gladly pay the extra  cash just to get the black bezels that  they prefer so with all that said there  are actually going to be some very good  reasons to go for the new macbook pro  over the air with the biggest one being  the 14 inch display with promotion and  just like that it now finally makes  sense for apple to keep the entry level  macbook pro around as a stepping stone  going up to the 2 000 m1 macbook pro  since the current 700 gap is way too  large to make any sense at all so with  that said let's get into my predictions  for the pricing of apple's entire 2022  macbook lineup we of course have the m1  macbook air which i think is going to  stick to the same exact 999 starting  price because it's still a great deal  and i think that's apple's magical  number for a starting macbook and then i  think the brand new redesigned m2  13-inch macbook air will be priced at  either 11.99 like what they did in 2018  or potentially up to 12.99 if they want  to raise their price points because of  supply chain and inflationary issues and  then of course you've got the m2 14-inch  macbook pro which i think will be priced  at either 13.99 or 14.99 and yes i know  that's a hundred to two hundred dollars  more expensive than the current m1 model  but if you think about it you're going  to be able to get that awesome new  design with the 14 inch mini led display  with 120hz promotion at five to six  hundred dollars less than the current  two thousand dollar m1 pro macbook pro  which i bet a lot of people would pay  for so this would essentially create a  smaller gap between the lower end m2  macbook pro and the 2000 14-inch macbook  pro just like in the past when the base  model was thirteen hundred dollars and  the high-end model was eighteen hundred  dollars and yes i fully believe that  apple is not going to be upgrading the  current 14 and 16 inch m1 pro macbook  pro models until  2023 so those will be staying in the  lineup next year but i do want to  emphasize that apple is going to make it  super tempting to just buy the 2 000  model because i fully expect the m2  macbook pro to start with only 256 gigs  of slower storage not the crazy 5000 to  7000 megabytes per second ssds that the  m1 pro models have and it's only gonna  have eight gigs of slower ram not the  insane 6200 megahertz lp ddr5x that the  m1 pro chip uses so just by upgrading to  a 512 gig ssd and 16 gigs of ram you'll  essentially be only 100 to 200 off of  the price of the high-end m1 pro macbook  pro depending on what they priced the m2  model at which is exactly what apple did  in the past with their intel max so if  you look at everything from this  perspective which is based on what apple  did in the past this new 2022 macbook  lineup makes total sense and this time  around it makes even more sense for  apple to have an entry-level macbook pro  so there you go those are my thoughts on  the new 2022 macbook lineup if you  totally disagree with me then go ahead  and comment your thoughts down below but  if you enjoyed this video go ahead and  click the circle above to subscribe for  more videos like this one and check out  one of those two right over there thanks  for watching and we'll see you in the  next video  [Music]

